From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Norman Herms <dockseed@proton.me>
Date: Mon, 12 Oct 2026 13:11:30 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: allwinner: a733: cubie-a7s: Describe the PMIC
 input supplies

The board is powered through the USB-C port J16. Its VBUS (VCC5V0)
passes the over-voltage switch U12 (SGM40666AS), which has no enable
from the SoC, and becomes VCC5V0_SYS. That rail feeds the VBUS switches
of the USB-C port J4 (U2) and of the USB-A port J8 (U10), both
SGM2576, and the DCIN pins of the AXP318W.

Inside the PMIC, PS is DCIN. PS feeds the inputs of all buck
converters (VIN19, VIN23, VIN45, VIN678), AIN156 and DLDOIN, and the
buck UP11 (ETA3521). UP11 makes LDO2V5-INPUT, the input of the BLDO and
CLDO groups. Its feedback divider, 30 kOhm over 10 kOhm on the 0.6 V
reference, sets 2.4 V.

Add VCC5V0_SYS and LDO2V5-INPUT as always-on fixed regulators. Make
VCC5V0_SYS the input of both VBUS switches and of the PMIC inputs that
PS feeds, and LDO2V5-INPUT the input of BLDOIN and CLDOIN. AIN234 comes
from ALDO1 and ELDOIN from DCDC9; neither is described here, so both
inputs stay out.

Tested on Radxa Cubie A7S: booted; the regulator tree shows the PMIC
regulators under vcc5v0-sys and vcc-pc under ldo2v5-input, with no new
deferred probe.

Assisted-by: LLM
---
 .../dts/allwinner/sun60i-a733-cubie-a7s.dts   | 42 +++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 42 insertions(+)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun60i-a733-cubie-a7s.dts b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun60i-a733-cubie-a7s.dts
index 6acd4c657b37..761ca15eab41 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun60i-a733-cubie-a7s.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun60i-a733-cubie-a7s.dts
@@ -84,6 +84,7 @@ reg_usb1_vbus: regulator-usb1-vbus {
 		regulator-max-microvolt = <5000000>;
 		gpio = <&r_pio 1 5 GPIO_ACTIVE_HIGH>; /* PM5 */
 		enable-active-high;
+		vin-supply = <&reg_vcc5v0_sys>;
 	};
 
 	/* WIFI_3V3 of the WiFi/BT module, load switch Q8 enabled by USB_WIFI_PWR (PM0) */
@@ -104,6 +105,34 @@ reg_usbc_vbus: regulator-usbc-vbus {
 		regulator-max-microvolt = <5000000>;
 		gpio = <&r_pio 0 2 GPIO_ACTIVE_HIGH>; /* PL2 */
 		enable-active-high;
+		vin-supply = <&reg_vcc5v0_sys>;
+	};
+
+	/*
+	 * VCC5V0_SYS: VBUS of the USB-C power input J16 (VCC5V0) behind the
+	 * over-voltage switch U12 (SGM40666AS), enabled by hardware alone.
+	 */
+	reg_vcc5v0_sys: regulator-vcc5v0-sys {
+		compatible = "regulator-fixed";
+		regulator-name = "vcc5v0-sys";
+		regulator-min-microvolt = <5000000>;
+		regulator-max-microvolt = <5000000>;
+		regulator-always-on;
+	};
+
+	/*
+	 * LDO2V5-INPUT, the input of the PMIC's BLDO and CLDO groups: buck UP11
+	 * (ETA3521) from PS, enabled by its input. The feedback divider
+	 * (30 kOhm over 10 kOhm on its 0.6 V reference) sets 2.4 V, not the
+	 * 2.5 V of the net name.
+	 */
+	reg_ldo2v5_input: regulator-ldo2v5-input {
+		compatible = "regulator-fixed";
+		regulator-name = "ldo2v5-input";
+		regulator-min-microvolt = <2400000>;
+		regulator-max-microvolt = <2400000>;
+		regulator-always-on;
+		vin-supply = <&reg_vcc5v0_sys>;
 	};
 };
 
@@ -319,6 +348,19 @@ axp318: pmic@36 {
 		interrupts-extended = <&nmi_intc 0 IRQ_TYPE_LEVEL_LOW>;
 		interrupt-controller;
 		#interrupt-cells = <1>;
+		/*
+		 * DCIN is VCC5V0_SYS. PS is DCIN inside the PMIC, and it feeds
+		 * the buck inputs, AIN156 and DLDOIN. AIN234 (from ALDO1) and
+		 * ELDOIN (from DCDC9) are left out: neither source is described.
+		 */
+		vin19-supply = <&reg_vcc5v0_sys>;
+		vin23-supply = <&reg_vcc5v0_sys>;
+		vin45-supply = <&reg_vcc5v0_sys>;
+		vin678-supply = <&reg_vcc5v0_sys>;
+		aldo156in-supply = <&reg_vcc5v0_sys>;
+		bldoin-supply = <&reg_ldo2v5_input>;
+		cldoin-supply = <&reg_ldo2v5_input>;
+		dldoin-supply = <&reg_vcc5v0_sys>;
 
 		regulators {
 			reg_dcdc1: dcdc1 {
